BT /F1 8 Tf 48 812 Td (RMS Operation) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (RMS Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 752.0 Td (The RMS \(Radio Management System\) is the companion desktop application for the radio firmware.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 739.0 Td (It provides a powerful and user-friendly way to configure, manage, and back up virtually every) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 726.0 Td (aspect of the radio without needing to navigate menus on the device itself.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 710.0 Td (Using the RMS, you can configure channels, groups, scanning behavior, band plans, APRS/GPS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 697.0 Td (features, power output, UI skins, key mappings, and more. Changes are made on the computer and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 684.0 Td (then written to the radio over a serial connection, making complex configuration tasks faster,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 671.0 Td (clearer, and far less error-prone than performing them directly on the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 655.0 Td (RMS versions are tightly coupled to firmware versions. Unless explicitly stated otherwise in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 642.0 Td (release post, users should always download and use the matching RMS version that corresponds to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 629.0 Td (the firmware installed on the radio. Mismatched versions may result in missing features or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 616.0 Td (incorrect behaviour.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 600.0 Td (Download links for the RMS are provided alongside firmware releases and are available for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 587.0 Td (Microsoft Windows, Linux, and macOS.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 571.0 m 547 571.0 l S
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 557.0 Td (RMS Operation Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 525.0 Td (The RMS is organized into a series of tabs, with each tab responsible for configuring a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 512.0 Td (specific aspect of radio operation. You can work with each tab independently, adjusting only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 499.0 Td (the settings you are interested in.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 483.0 Td (There is also a Codeplug tab, which allows you to combine many common configurations into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 470.0 Td (single file. This is useful for creating backups, sharing configurations, or moving a complete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 457.0 Td (setup between radios. See: RMS  ->  Codeplug) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 441.0 Td (An important concept is that the RMS does not immediately apply changes to the radio. Instead,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (it maintains its own internal copy of the radio?s storage, think of this as a working draft.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 412.0 Td (As you change settings in the RMS, you are modifying this draft copy, not the radio itself. To) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 399.0 Td (apply those changes to the radio, you must explicitly write them.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 383.0 m 547 383.0 l S
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 369.0 Td (Configuration Files) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 337.0 Td (All configuration files loaded and saved by the RMS use the .csv \(Comma-Separated Values\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 324.0 Td (format. This is a plain-text format that can be opened and viewed with common tools such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 311.0 Td (spreadsheet applications or text editors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 295.0 Td (Using a text-based format was a deliberate design choice. Files with clearly labeled,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 282.0 Td (human-readable fields are far easier to inspect, edit, back up, and troubleshoot than opaque) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 269.0 Td (binary files.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 253.0 Td (For power users, this makes advanced manipulation and automation straightforward. For everyday) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 240.0 Td (users, these files behave just like any other configuration file; load them, save them, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 227.0 Td (move them around as needed, without requiring any special knowledge of how they work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 214.0 Td (internally.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 198.0 m 547 198.0 l S
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 184.0 Td (RMS Tabs - Common Controls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 152.0 Td (Most RMS tabs include the same four buttons. Understanding what these do will make using the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 139.0 Td (RMS much easier.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 119.0 Td (Load) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 92.2 Td (Loads a previously saved .csv file into the RMS. This updates the RMS?s working copy and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 79.2 Td (on-screen settings, but does not change anything on the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 285.5 28 Td (Page 5) Tj ET
Q
endstream
