BT /F1 8 Tf 48 812 Td (RMS Operation) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (Save) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 757.2 Td (Creates a .csv file from the current RMS working copy. This is useful for backups or sharing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 744.2 Td (settings. This action does not read anything from the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 724.2 Td (Read) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 697.4 Td (Reads the relevant settings from the radio into the RMS. This synchronizes the RMS working copy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 684.4 Td (with what is currently stored on the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 664.4 Td (Write) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 637.6 Td (Writes the RMS working copy back to the radio. This is the step that actually applies your) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 624.6 Td (changes to the device.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 608.6 m 547 608.6 l S
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 594.6 Td (Common Tab Tasks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 562.6 Td (Here's some examples of common tasks you might perform with the RMS tabs.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 542.6 Td (Backup of tab configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 515.8 Td (- Switch to the tab responsible for the settings you wish to backup.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 499.8 Td (- Click Read to synchronize the RMS to the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 483.8 Td (- Click Save to create and save a .csv file to your computer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 463.8 Td (Restoring tab configuration from backup) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 437.0 Td (- Switch to the tab responsible for the settings you wish to restore.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 421.0 Td (- Click Load and select the .csv file created previously.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 405.0 Td (- Click Write to apply the backup to the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 285.5 28 Td (Page 6) Tj ET
Q
endstream
