BT /F1 8 Tf 48 812 Td (RMS Serial) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (RMS Serial Ports & Baud Rate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 757.2 Td (Communication between the RMS and the radio occurs over a serial programming cable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 741.2 Td (- \(RT-880 Only\) Although the RT-880 includes a USB-C port, a standard USB-C to USB-A cable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 728.2 Td (only supports battery charging and cannot be used for data communication.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 712.2 Td (A USB cable specifically designed for the RT-880 or RT-950 is required. These are available) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 699.2 Td (from Radtel and various online marketplaces. Search for: RT-880 Programming Cable. RT-950 Pro) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 686.2 Td (Programming Cable. Note: The RT-950 Pro generally comes supplied with a programming cable in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 673.2 Td (the box.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 657.2 Td (It is recommended to use cables with quality chipsets, such as CH340. Avoid cheaper cables) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 644.2 Td (using Prolific chipsets, as they are often unreliable.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 628.2 m 547 628.2 l S
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 614.2 Td (Port / Baud Controls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 587.4 Td (The bottom-right corner of the RMS application window contains the serial configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 574.4 Td (controls. These are labeled Port/Baud and consist of two drop-down selectors.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 558.4 Td (text) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48.0 538.4 Td (Port Dropdown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 515.5 Td (Displays all serial ports currently detected by your computer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 499.5 Td (Select the port associated with your RT-880 programming cable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 483.5 Td (If multiple ports are listed, an easy way to identify the correct one is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 467.5 Td (1. Open the port dropdown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 451.5 Td (2. Unplug the programming cable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 435.5 Td (3. Note which port disappears) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 419.5 Td (4. Plug the cable back in and select that port) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48.0 399.5 Td (Baud Dropdown) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 376.6 Td (Allows selection of the communication speed used between RMS and the radio.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 360.6 Td (Available baud rates range from:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 344.6 Td (- 38,400 up to 518,400) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 328.6 Td (The maximum reliable speed depends on:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 312.6 Td (- Cable quality) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 296.6 Td (- Radio tolerances) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 280.6 Td (- Computer hardware and drivers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 264.6 Td (Some experimentation may be required to determine the fastest stable setting.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 248.6 m 547 248.6 l S
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 234.6 Td (Firmware Flashing Note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 207.8 Td (The configurable baud rate does not apply to firmware flashing. Firmware flashing always uses a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 194.8 Td (fixed baud rate of 115,200.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 178.8 m 547 178.8 l S
