BT /F1 8 Tf 48 812 Td (Squelch Menu) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (Squelch Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 752.0 Td (Squelch is a system designed to mute the main speaker until a valid signal is received. nicFW?s) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 739.0 Td (squelch implementation is significantly more advanced than that of most radios and allows for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 726.0 Td (fine-grained control over how and when audio is unmuted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 710.0 Td (nicFW squelch operates based on two independent factors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 694.0 Td (- Signal strength \(RSSI\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 678.0 Td (- Received noise level \(ExNoise\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 662.0 Td (For squelch to open, the signal strength must rise above a configured threshold and the noise) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 649.0 Td (level must fall below its threshold. For squelch to close, the signal must drop back below its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 636.0 Td (threshold and the noise level must rise again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 620.0 Td (While the Squelch Menu is open, the menu?s Extra Info field displays real-time numerical values) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 607.0 Td (for the current channel or frequency?s RSSI and ExNoise levels. These live readings can be used) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 594.0 Td (to determine optimal values for several squelch parameters and Signal Floor calibration.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 578.0 m 547 578.0 l S
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 564.0 Td (Squelch Menu Options) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (Level) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 501.2 Td (- Available Values: 0 \(Off\) to 9) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 485.2 Td (- Default Value: 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 469.2 Td (Controls the primary signal-strength requirement for opening squelch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 453.2 Td (- 0 \(Off\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 437.2 Td (Disables squelch entirely; the speaker remains unmuted at all times.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 421.2 Td (- 1) Tj ET
