BT /F1 8 Tf 48 812 Td (Storage Deferral) Tj ET
BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (Storage Deferral Overview) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (Note: Only the RT-880 uses storage deferral. The RT-950 Pro) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 727.2 Td (does not need it as it has a software power on/off system.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 706.4 Td (Thus this section is only relevant for the RT-880.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 679.6 Td (Like a PC, smartphone, or tablet, the radio contains non-volatile storage used to preserve its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 666.6 Td (settings and operational state. Users generally expect the radio to return to the same state it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 653.6 Td (was in when powered off, which means that nearly every user action must be saved, channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 640.6 Td (changes, frequency adjustments, and configuration updates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 624.6 Td (However, the storage device used in the radio has a limited write endurance, typically rated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 611.6 Td (for approximately 100,000 write cycles. Exceeding this limit can result in permanent storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 598.6 Td (failure, rendering the radio unusable.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 582.6 Td (To protect the storage device and extend the radio?s usable lifespan, nicFW employs an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 569.6 Td (aggressive strategy to minimize write operations. This mechanism is referred to as Storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 556.6 Td (Deferral.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 536.6 Td (How It Works) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 509.8 Td (When a change would normally require a write to storage, the update is first placed into a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 496.8 Td (temporary buffer rather than being written immediately. Multiple changes can then accumulate in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 483.8 Td (this buffer and are later committed to storage in a single write operation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 467.8 Td (By consolidating many small writes into fewer large ones, Storage Deferral dramatically reduces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 454.8 Td (the total number of write cycles over the lifetime of the device.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 438.8 Td (The amount of time changes remain buffered before being written is user-configurable. See: Main) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 425.8 Td (Menu  ->  Advanced  ->  SPI Deferral) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 405.8 Td (Impact on User Experience) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 379.0 Td (When there are pending changes waiting to be written to storage, a red warning triangle is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 366.0 Td (displayed on the main screen. If the radio is powered off while this indicator is visible:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 350.0 Td (- The pending changes will be discarded) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 334.0 Td (- No corruption or damage will occur) Tj ET
