BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 614.2 Td (Why does the frequency mode scan start lower than the start) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 593.4 Td (frequency I configured?) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 566.6 Td (When performing a frequency \(VFO\) mode scan with Ultra Scan enabled, the scanner must first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 553.6 Td (establish a reliable noise floor so it can correctly identify potential signals.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 537.6 Td (Ultra Scan does this by maintaining a rolling minimum of the noise levels from the last 16) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 524.6 Td (scanned frequencies. This keeps the noise floor local and relevant to the part of the spectrum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 511.6 Td (currently being scanned, which greatly improves detection accuracy and speed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 495.6 Td (However, this approach has a small side effect: at the very beginning of a scan, the noise) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 482.6 Td (floor has not yet been fully initialized or localized. The first 16 frequencies would otherwise) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 469.6 Td (be evaluated using incomplete or inaccurate noise data.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 453.6 Td (To avoid this, the scanner automatically shifts the effective start frequency downward by 16) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 440.6 Td (steps. This gives Ultra Scan enough data to establish a proper noise baseline before reaching) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 427.6 Td (your configured start frequency.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 411.6 Td (As a result, the scan appears to begin slightly below the start frequency you set, but by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 398.6 Td (time it reaches your configured range, the noise floor is fully settled and signal detection is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 385.6 Td (accurate.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 369.6 m 547 369.6 l S
