BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (CAT Commands) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 748.0 Td (Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 721.2 Td (CAT \(Computer Aided Transceiver\) allows a radio to be remotely controlled by a host machine) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 708.2 Td (over a serial connection using structured command/response messages.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 692.2 Td (This is distinct from the Remote tab of the RMS, which functions as a screen and keypad) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 679.2 Td (mirroring system. CAT operates using a command-driven control paradigm instead.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 659.2 Td (Connection and framing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 632.4 Td (Commands are sent as plain text at 38,400 baud over the standard programming interface and must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 619.4 Td (be terminated with ONLY a \(carriage return, ASCII 13\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 599.4 Td (Responses and prompt) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 572.6 Td (Each command returns a text response that is one of the following:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 556.6 Td (- an error) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 540.6 Td (- an acknowledgement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 524.6 Td (- a reply to a query) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 508.6 Td (Responses are terminated with \(ASCII 13, 10\) and followed by the command prompt \(if E 2 is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 495.6 Td (active\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 479.6 Td (cmd:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 463.6 Td (Each command described below documents its expected responses.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 443.6 Td (Communication check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 416.8 Td (Sending a single with no command returns only the prompt \(providing E 2 is active\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 400.8 Td (cmd:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 384.8 Td (Implementations are encouraged to do this to confirm valid communication before sending) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 371.8 Td (commands.) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 355.8 m 547 355.8 l S
BT /F3 9 Tf 62.0 345.8 Td (Warning:? Note: The list below documents all currently available CAT commands.) Tj ET
BT /F3 9 Tf 62.0 331.1 Td (Additional commands may be introduced in future revisions based on user requests.) Tj ET
BT /F2 16 Tf 48.0 312.4 Td (RX Frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 285.6 Td (Command Format:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 269.6 Td (- F [MMMMKKKHHH]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 253.6 Td (Command Responses:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 237.6 Td (- F MMMMKKKHHH) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 221.6 Td (To indicate the actual frequency that was tuned or the reply to a query. Sometimes it can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 208.6 Td (changed by frequency limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 192.6 Td (- E Invalid Frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 176.6 Td (If the frequency was incorrectly formatted or outside the valid range of 18 to 1300 MHz) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 160.6 Td (Sets or queries the currently active VFO's receive frequency in Hz.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 48.0 140.6 Td (Setting the RX Frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 117.7 Td (- If the VFO is in Channel or Group mode, the selected pre-programmed channel?s RX frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 104.7 Td (will be permanently updated to the specified value.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 88.7 Td (- The TX frequency automatically follows the RX frequency and preserves any configured) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 75.7 Td (offset.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 285.5 28 Td (Page 111) Tj ET
Q
