BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (Serial Protocol Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 752.0 Td (Communication between HOST and RADIO is performed over a USB serial programming cable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 739.0 Td (specifically designed for the RT-880. The default communication speed is 38,400 baud, but this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 726.0 Td (can be changed dynamically using a command packet \(see below\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 710.0 Td (All communication uses a synchronous packet-based protocol, with the exception of Remote Mode,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 697.0 Td (which uses its own asynchronous protocol. The serial protocol is used to control link speed and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 684.0 Td (to read from or write to the radio?s flash storage.) Tj ET
