BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 784.0 Td (Remote Protocol Overview) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 752.0 Td (Remote Mode uses a datagram-based packet protocol. Communication is unacknowledged \(except for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 739.0 Td (PING\), meaning packets are not guaranteed to arrive and are not retried.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 723.0 Td (The radio's display is 240x320 pixels in a portrait orientation. Implementations should ideally) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 710.0 Td (keep the key controls, display mirror and any other connection based controls all on the screen) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 697.0 Td (together without having to scroll.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 681.0 Td (Once Remote Mode is active:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 665.0 Td (- The radio no longer responds to normal serial commands) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 649.0 Td (- Storage read/write operations are disabled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 60.0 633.0 Td (- Only Remote protocol packets are processed) Tj ET
0.55 w 48 617.0 m 547 617.0 l S
