BT /F2 20 Tf 48.0 285.0 Td (Packet Checksums) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 253.0 Td (The last byte of all display packets sent by the radio is a checksum. The checksum is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 240.0 Td (calculated by adding every byte of the packet other than the checksum byte itself. The sum is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 227.0 Td (an 8-bit additive checksum, so it wraps at 0xFF. The host should calculate this checksum and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 48.0 214.0 Td (check it matches the checksum byte sent at the end of the packet.) Tj ET
